Sync progress counters and a nested-read fix for get_transaction_history

Applies to ChainSafe/WebZjs a50df944c32243cb8da9f86e7d52cb65ac926439
(scripts/build-webzjs.sh applies patches/webzjs/*.patch in order).

1. WebWallet.sync_progress(): lock-free counters for the running sync pass.
   Wallet::sync holds the database write lock for the whole pass, so
   get_wallet_summary cannot answer until it ends. A BlockCache wrapper
   (src/progress.rs) counts blocks as zcash_client_backend::sync::run moves
   them through insert (downloaded), the scanner's first walk (visited) and
   the next batch's insert (scanned = committed). sync_progress() only reads
   atomics, so it answers mid-pass. Adds async-trait (already in Cargo.lock
   through zcash_client_memory) to webzjs-wallet's dependencies.

2. get_transaction_history took db.read() and, holding it, called
   get_wallet_summary(), which takes db.read() again. tokio's RwLock is
   write-preferring: if sync asks for the write lock between the two reads,
   the second read queues behind the writer, the writer waits for the first
   read, and every later wallet call hangs. The fix reuses the held guard.

